WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.062
CTEs are not automatically better.

00:00:03.062 --> 00:00:06.407
A short query may be clearer without one.

00:00:06.407 --> 00:00:10.472
A CTE also does not repair unclear grain.

00:00:10.472 --> 00:00:13.977
And it does not automatically make a query faster.

00:00:13.977 --> 00:00:18.837
Use named stages when they improve reasoning and maintainability.

00:00:18.837 --> 00:00:25.932
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:25.932 --> 00:00:34.447
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a new

00:00:34.447 --> 00:00:41.520
block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
